    <string name="privacy">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_text">Grabadora has no ads or analytics. The microphone is used only while you record, when you tap the red button; the AI can never record. Recordings are kept only on this phone, in Music › Grabadora, and the settings, marks and waveforms stay out of cloud backups. Only if you turn on MCP Mode can the AI you connect with a token see the names, dates, lengths, sizes and marks of your recordings and, with a read-and-write token, rename them through the relay. The audio leaves only if you turn on «Let the AI listen to recordings» (in MCP Mode), so a model can transcribe it. Only you delete, on the phone.</string>
    <string name="mcp_settings_hint">Your AI (Claude, ChatGPT…) or Gateway Hub see and rename your recordings.</string>
    <string name="mcp_title">MCP mode</string>
    <string name="mcp_enable">Turn on MCP</string>
    <string name="mcp_enable_hint">Works while Grabadora is open or in the background.</string>
    <string name="mcp_enable_by_hub">Managed by Gateway Hub while «Redirect to Hub» is on.</string>
    <string name="mcp_online">Connected to the internet</string>
    <string name="mcp_connecting">Connecting…</string>
    <string name="mcp_offline">Offline</string>
    <string name="mcp_redirect">Redirect to Hub</string>
    <string name="mcp_redirect_hint">Gateway Hub manages permissions, expiry and support. No need to turn MCP on.</string>
    <string name="mcp_listen">Let the AI listen to recordings</string>
    <string name="mcp_listen_hint">So a model can transcribe them to text: with this on, an AI with a read-and-write token can ask for a recording\'s audio (with its date and time, length and size). Off, the audio never leaves.</string>
